{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"3a59e8f2a1fee564c565d69eeb1ebda18034089cf9d069ad94336b661890aa03","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_11833097691e344aa47b9c243c7b49027589d501087083d4bf1d868a6d6f41cc","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a significant methodological contribution to multi-view representation learning by unifying the probabilistic interpretation of CCA with the variational inference framework of deep generative models. The proposed VCCA and VCCA-private models offer a principled, end-to-end trainable alternative to previous deep CCA variants, addressing the lack of a generative model in prior work. The empirical results demonstrate competitive performance across diverse domains, with the added benefit of sample generation and disentanglement of shared and private variables, which provides a deeper understanding of the data structure.","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_identity_sha256":"56ca5c71a10bb0fa6d93e752c44f8cfde6ea0f56a3383702f83387459e1b6d79","prompt_identity_sha256":"14a5df441dbb3865d57ebe470cc8cc0f3f789d55ded195d764126589b3b9121e","raw_response_sha256":"4a12cd4fc68eca87cc36c3f6f322a3344f7700c0afa3b2875cb35a63b8ae26d4","request_identity_sha256":"e0008d6c86ba5bdb55179675a8aae6f661f2d87e16bdb1081fcde7f177de30d9","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"b821e43be712e80f9ef8a1c1bd694e1cef6c4afedb10f9131936b7e1cfdffab5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-007","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The work addresses a fundamental problem in multi-view representation learning by providing a deep generative model that extends the probabilistic interpretation of linear CCA. This approach is broadly significant as it bridges the gap between classical statistical methods and modern deep learning, offering a framework that can be applied to various multi-view settings. The ability to model the joint distribution of views through shared latent variables has the potential to influence research in representation learning, generative modeling, and multi-modal learning.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-030","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates the applicability of the proposed method across three distinct domains: image-image (Noisy MNIST), speech-articulation (XRMB), and image-text (MIR-Flickr). In each domain, the method is evaluated on a specific downstream task (classification, phonetic recognition, and topic classification, respectively). The results show that VCCA and VCCA-private are competitive with or superior to existing deep multi-view methods, indicating strong domain-specific impact. The ability to generate samples and disentangle shared/private variables is particularly relevant for exploratory analysis and understanding data structure in these fields.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-036","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper reports performance improvements over several strong baselines, including DCCA, DCCAE, and MVAE. On the Noisy MNIST dataset, VCCA-private achieves a classification error rate of 2.4%, which is comparable to the best previous approach (DCCAE at 2.2%) and significantly better than DCCA (2.9%) and MVAE (11.7%). On the XRMB dataset, VCCA-private achieves a mean phone error rate of 25.2%, which is competitive with DCCA and DCCAE (25.4%) and better than the baseline MFCCs (37.6%). On the MIR-Flickr dataset, VCCA-private achieves a test mAP of 0.586, outperforming DCCA and DCCAE (0.573) and the image feature baseline (0.480). These results suggest that the proposed method offers a meaningful improvement over the state of the art, particularly in its ability to generate samples and disentangle variables.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper does not explicitly discuss the societal or real-world impact of the proposed method beyond its application to specific benchmarks. While the ability to generate high-quality samples and disentangle shared/private variables could have practical benefits in areas such as data augmentation, exploratory data analysis, and understanding complex multi-modal data, the paper does not elaborate on these potential applications or their broader implications. There is no discussion of fairness, environmental impact, or other societal considerations.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"4e95825990a35a7db6965f3230aaa2b438af99162e15f9e8b889f445cc1fc25c","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_ordinal":89,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"4a12cd4fc68eca87cc36c3f6f322a3344f7700c0afa3b2875cb35a63b8ae26d4","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"db50c6ff2ac7610e483c082738cc46558312cd95c477140fd799d8e4bc64b64d","request_identity_sha256":"e0008d6c86ba5bdb55179675a8aae6f661f2d87e16bdb1081fcde7f177de30d9","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":926,"prompt_tokens":21125,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":22051},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"e0008d6c86ba5bdb55179675a8aae6f661f2d87e16bdb1081fcde7f177de30d9","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}